User "2" -- "0..*" Conversation : participants
User "1" -- "0..*" Announcement : author
User "0..1" -- "0..*" Event : author

note as N1
  <b>Conventions</b>
  • Every class also carries <i>created_at</i> / <i>updated_at</i> (Laravel timestamps) unless noted.
  • Foreign keys are shown as attributes (<i>*_id</i>) exactly as they exist in the database;
    only the structurally important associations are drawn to keep the diagram readable
    (e.g. <i>academic_year_id</i> / <i>semester_id</i> / <i>subject_id</i> on Grade, Exam, Homework, Lesson, Quiz…).
  • Every class outside <b>Tenancy & Billing</b> (except PersonalAccessToken) uses the
    <i>BelongsToSchool</i> trait: a global <i>TenantScope</i> filters by <i>school_id</i> and
    fills it on create from <i>TenantContext</i>. That implicit <b>School 1 — * X</b> composition
    is therefore not repeated for each class.
  • Roles are not subclasses: a <i>User</i> has a role and optionally a Student or Teacher profile.
end note
N1 .. PKG_TENANCY
